## 5. Kernel orientation (read from src/ this session — description of existing code, not insight)

Reduction core, `src/net.c`: one step is `interact(o, v)` (~1806) — an active pair is one operation
meeting the single value it consumes; `redex` (~314) drops two-value or two-operation pairs as dead
wire; `l->steps++` ticks once per interact. Universal rules before any type rule: `O_ERA` erase,
`O_DUP` duplicate (lazy, one level — the O(1) share; a `V_REF` box read is a refcount bump +
one-level copy, ~1879), `O_SUBST` dimension-substitution. Laziness is default: `O_FWD` parked read is
"not a step" (~1808); `unbuilt(v)` builds on demand (~1875); `V_GLOBAL` copies a definition's body in
lazily and parks if not ready (~1866). Open terms reduce: an eliminator meeting `V_UNK` erases its
branches and passes the neutral through (~1886). Lock-free parallelism (`link`/`publish`, ~334-376):
two principals rendezvous through a variable cell by atomic exchange (first arrival wins); every wire
and made-pair of a rewrite is deferred and published only when the whole rewrite completes, so no
thread sees a half-written cell; work-stealing deques carry the pairs.

Content-addressed store, `src/store.c`: a checked definition's key is SHA-256 of the canonical
type+term — binders nameless (`@k` de Bruijn), each dependency replaced by its key (`G<key>`/`D<key>`,
constructors/fields `C<key>.i`/`F<key>.i`), multiplicities kept, names/files/positions excluded
(`key_def`, ~618) — so one definition has one key on every machine. `.cubical-store/<key>/check` is a
per-checker certificate; `names` is an append-only `name key time` log.

